{"parentUuid":"49753be3-019c-48f0-87fb-53347539deb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0184iUxBzEX4iJXw1dSi3XDi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full picture:\n\n**The key insight:**\n\n`anytype-cli.service` runs `anytype serve -q --listen-address 127.0.0.1:31012` — it's listening on port **31012** (HTTP API), NOT port 31010 (gRPC)!\n\nWait, but `ss -tlnp | grep 31010` showed something listening on port 31010 too. Let me re-read... yes, both ports are listening from the same process (anytype pid 160472):\n- Port 31010: gRPC API\n- Port 31012: HTTP API\n\n\n- The service restarts daily at 22:01 UTC (07:01 JST), which is exactly when the daily report runs — this is the `anytype-prestart.sh` script killing the old process and starting fresh.\n- The gRPC sync failure at 01:34 UTC happens because `anytype-workspace-sync` is still pointing to an old space from claw-bot-v2, while the restarted `anytype-cli` is now using a different account entirely.\n\nSo the real issue is that the migration from gRPC to HTTP API was intentional — the daily reports work fine through the new HTTP path, but the old gRPC-based round-trip test is still trying to run against a deprecated service with stale configuration. Nothing actually broke in production; the test is just using an outdated approach that was already phased out.\n\nThe `anytype-workspace-sync` service is disabled and was only manually started for this test attempt at 01:34 UTC, where it failed. The gRPC space ID in the test belongs to the `claw-bot-v2` account from the March setup, but the currently running `anytype-cli.service` (which started at 22:01 UTC via cron) might be logged in under a different account, causing the authentication mismatch.\n\nThe real issue is likely that the gRPC sync service is trying to access a space that the current `anytype serve` instance doesn't have credentials for—either because the service restarted with a different account, the space ID was always misconfigured, or the HTTP/gRPC port configuration changed. Port 31010 is definitely listening with the anytype process, so gRPC should be reachable, but the authentication layer is the bottleneck.\n\nActually, I think the core problem is simpler: the `anytype-workspace-sync` service was deprecated during the migration to HTTP API and its space ID configuration was never updated. It's been failing silently while the daily reports work fine because they use the HTTP API directly and don't depend on that deprecated service at all. The round-trip test never actually worked after the migration—it just looked like it did. And checking the logs, `anytype-cli` did restart at 22:01 UTC, which aligns with when things started failing.\n\nNow I'm realizing the timing is important: `anytype-workspace-sync` ran at 01:34 UTC, which was after the restart, so it was running against the new instance. The prestart script killed the old process and started fresh, but the new instance apparently never re-discovered or re-synced the old space from the coordinator. By the time the sync job ran 3.5 hours later, the space still wasn't available to it.\n\nLooking at the port bindings, both gRPC on 31010 and the HTTP API on 31012 are coming from the same `anytype serve` process (PID 160472), so gRPC is definitely available. But when `anytype-workspace-sync` tries to access space `bafyreibwatfpuq23i74...`, it fails saying the space doesn't exist — which suggests the anytype-cli instance might be using a different data directory or configuration than expected.\n\nComparing the space IDs, the current \"Rob New Place\" space is `bafyreig4q7t3vt7b7zmvfv3emj7jfrvjamuhu4crws3dhn3uaxhh3u37k4.10piockh34xft` from the March setup, but the gRPC sync is configured with `REDACTED.35fpfsusofs1o` — these are completely different space IDs. The sync was never pointing at the right space, or `bafyreibwatfpuq23i74...` is an older test space that no longer exists in the current anytype instance.\n\nSo the daily reports work fine because they use the HTTP API, but the round-trip test with gRPC and the objectmap has been broken since the migration — the `anytype-workspace-sync` service is disabled and configured with a stale space ID that doesn't exist anymore, so the objectmap never gets updated with the `claude-test` entry. Either the service needs its space ID corrected or the test needs to be redesigned to use the HTTP API path instead.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3781,"cache_read_input_tokens":32972,"output_tokens":2640,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3781,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2640,"cache_read_input_tokens":32972,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3781},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaMkN1TUD77tC6t5WDwY9","type":"assistant","uuid":"e179bd4e-ff11-421b-9f2a-19d391f10315","timestamp":"2026-04-24T01:44:27.998Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/rob/Documents/openclaw-workspace","sessionId":"316718bd-c95e-4dbb-ab74-6f7e7e2ac00c","version":"2.1.118","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e179bd4e-ff11-421b-9f2a-19d391f10315","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0184iUxBzEX4iJXw1dSi3XDi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The answer is clear now. **Nothing broke for the daily reports** — those are on a completely different path. What's broken is the *round-trip test*, and it's been broken since the migration away from gRPC. Here's the full picture:\n\n## Two separate pipelines\n\n**Daily reports (WORKING):**\n```\nCron 22:01 UTC → daily-report-api.sh → HTTP API :31012 → AnyType ✓\n```\nThis worked at 07:00 JST exactly because the `anytype-cli` service restarted at **22:01:18 UTC** (triggered by `anytype-prestart.sh`) and the daily report cron fired right on schedule.\n\n**Round-trip test (BROKEN):**\n```\nFile in /root/anytype-workspace/ → anytype-workspace-sync (gRPC) → AnyType ✗\n```\n\n## Why the gRPC path fails\n\n`anytype-workspace-sync` is **disabled** — it was intentionally deprecated when you migrated to the HTTP API (commit `676a5a9`). It ran manually at 01:34 UTC for the test and failed on every object with:\n\n```\nspace not exists (UNKNOWN_ERROR)\n```\n\nIt's targeting space `bafyreibwatfpuq23i74...` but the current `anytype-cli` (which is `anytype serve --listen-address 127.0.0.1:31012`) doesn't have that space — it's a stale/wrong space ID in the old sync service config.\n\n## Summary\n\n| | Daily Reports | Round-trip test |\n|--|--|--|\n| Transport | HTTP API (:31012) | gRPC (:31010) |\n| Service | `anytype-cli.service` (enabled) | `anytype-workspace-sync` (disabled) |\n| Status | Working | Broken — stale space ID, deprecated path |\n| Objectmap | Not used | Required, never written |\n\nThe objectmap will never get the `claude-test` entry via this path. The round-trip test needs to be rewritten to use the HTTP API — same as the daily reports. Want me to do that?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1