{"parentUuid":"db74ebf9-6d86-431f-b8a6-b9e87abba41b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0133tL2YfP8uDNUGVVhDgpZ8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll write the workspace sync script that uses HTTP API. I'll deploy it to the VPS, run it once to sync the test file, then update the objectmap.\n\nLet me write a proper Python-based script for this since it's more reliable for JSON handling. I'll write it to `/root/scripts/workspace-sync-api.sh`.\n\nThen I'll post a note to AnyType explaining what changed, for OC to read.\n\nLet me think about what the script needs to do:\n1. Read objectmap JSON\n2. For each .md file in workspace:\n   - Get the key (filename without .md)\n   - Check if it's in the objectmap\n   - If it is, optionally update (or skip if content hasn't changed)\n   - If not, create via HTTP API and add to objectmap\n3. Save updated objectmap\n\nI'll make it a bash script using python3 inline for JSON manipulation, keeping it consistent with the existing daily-report-api.sh style. For updates, I need to check whether the AnyType HTTP API supports PATCH or PUT endpoints — the daily report just POSTs new objects, so I should verify if there's an update mechanism available.\n\nLooking at the objectmap structure, it maps files to object IDs, so if a file already has an entry, I should update that object rather than create a duplicate. I'll implement both create and update paths using POST for new objects and PATCH for existing ones. For the OC notification, I'll document that the gRPC service is being replaced with this new HTTP-based sync script, and note that the round-trip test now works through the API.\n\nWriting the sync script...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2129,"cache_read_input_tokens":45233,"output_tokens":1735,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_